# Vauxhall Vectra B saloon, 1995-2002.
#
# The first Vectra sold in Britain: the Cavalier nameplate was dropped in
# October 1995 and the Opel Vectra A car of 1988-95 was never a Vauxhall, so
# this is the earliest Vectra object. Sold from October 1995 to March 2002.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_Vectra
#
# Dimensions 4.480 x 1.710 x 1.420 m, wheelbase 2.640 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a TRUE level side elevation, but of an ESTATE
# and a late car; the saloon rear is taken from the other views and the body
# difference is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no Vauxhall colour list was read. White, Red, Blue and
# Silver are plain names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
#
# Speed 195 km/h. Comfort 75/292, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 75. Classes 1,2.
# Dates: intro October 1995; retires staggered 2008-2011 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-vectra-b.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-vectra-b.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-vectra-b/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the pre-facelift UK saloon is modelled. The level side
# photograph is a late ESTATE and was used only for the axles and the forward
# profile; the saloon rear comes from oblique saloon views and a same-body
# Opel saloon photograph used for geometry only. Trim and lens internals are
# simplified.


obj=citycar
name=VauxhallVectraB(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=1995
intro_month=10
retire_year=2011
retire_month=6
speed=195
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=75
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=292

